ull":"BlackRock TCP Capital Corp. is a business development company specializing in direct equity and debt investments in middle-market, small businesses, debt securities, senior secured loans, junior loans, originated loans, mezzanine, senior debt instruments, bonds, and secondary-market investments. It typically invests in communication services, public relations services, television, wireless telecommunication services, apparel, textile mills, restaurants, retailing, energy, oil and gas extraction, Patent owners and Lessors, Federal and Federally- Sponsored Credit agencies, insurance, hospital and healthcare centers, Biotechnology, engineering services, heavy electrical equipment, tax accounting, scientific and related consulting services, charter freight air transportation, Information technology consulting, application hosting services, software diagram and design, computer aided design, communication equipment, electronics manufacturing equipment, computer components, chemicals. It seeks to invest in the United States. The fund typically invests in debt between $10 million and $35 million in companies with enterprise values between $100 million and $1500 million including complex situations. It prefers to make equity investments in companies for an ownership stake.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jason A. Mehring | Chairman & CEO | Age 54","financial_summary":["BlackRock TCP Capital Corp. is a small-cap financial services business with a $345M market cap.","Management returns a meaningful 28.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 389% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Blackrock Tcp Capital (TCPC) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/blackrock-tcp-capital-tcpc-said-211439776.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793999679.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"BlackRock TCP Capital Corp (TCPC) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: NAV Slides on Portfolio ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/blackrock-tcp-capital-corp-tcpc-091416992.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793956456.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"BlackRock TCP (TCPC) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/blackrock-tcp-tcpc-q3-2026-203102000.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793911357.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"BlackRock TCP Capital declares $0.17 dividend whil